Feature: slice-3 / register-therapist-google
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-3
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.1 + §13.2 (therapist social path)
Manual op #64 (Firebase Console Google + account linking): DONE per user.

What was built
==============
- src/components/register/SocialButtons.tsx — shared "Continue with
  Google" component for both register pages. On click:
    1. auth.signInWithGoogle() (popup) — already wired in feature 4.
    2. identityClient.getUserByFirebaseUID({firebaseUid: user.uid}).
    3. Existing user → window.location → app.superwizor.ai/login.
    4. ConnectError.NotFound → redirect to /register/<flow>/finish
       with ?firstName / lastName / email from the Google profile.
    5. Other ConnectError → surface as inline alert (don't proceed
       to finish-profile because we'd risk a duplicate user row).
  Includes brand-styled monochrome Google "G" mark inline SVG so we
  don't pull a separate icon dep. "or" divider separates social from
  email path.
- src/lib/register/schema.ts — therapistFinishSchema (zod) covering
  the minimal post-OAuth fields: names + modality + ui_language +
  optional title/phone + ToS.
- src/components/register/TherapistFinishForm.tsx — client form
  pre-filled from query (firstName / lastName). Submit calls
  identityClient.createUser({role=THERAPIST, ...}) using the
  still-signed-in Firebase user, then optionally updateProfile for
  modality + title + phone + marketing consent, then bounces
  straight to app.superwizor.ai/login (Google sign-in marks
  emailVerified=true server-side; no need for the
  /verify-email interstitial).
- src/app/[locale]/register/therapist/finish/page.tsx — dynamic
  route reading searchParams for the personalised "Witaj
  {firstName}" greeting (falls back to a generic subhead if the
  user landed here without query, e.g. via reload).
- Wired SocialButtons into
  src/app/[locale]/register/therapist/page.tsx above the email
  form.
- messages/{pl,en}.json — added therapist.finishMetaTitle /
  finishTitle / finishSubhead / finishGenericSubhead keys.

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table now includes
   `/[locale]/register/therapist/finish` (dynamic ƒ — uses
   searchParams).

2. HTTP smoke (after .next/dev wipe + Preview restart):
     /register/therapist                                                                            → 200
     /register/therapist/finish?firstName=Anna&lastName=Kowalska&email=anna@example.com             → 200

3. Puppeteer screenshots:
   - register-pl-full.png: Therapist register page now shows the
     "Kontynuuj z Google" Ember-on-frost-5 button at the top with
     the Google G mark, "LUB" Roboto-Mono divider, then the
     existing email form below. PL diacritics correct.
   - finish-pl-full.png: Finish-profile page with "Witaj Anna.
     Wybierz nurt terapeutyczny…" personalised subhead. First
     name + last name pre-filled with "Anna" / "Kowalska" from
     query. Modality select + UI language radio (Polski selected)
     + optional title + optional phone + ToS + marketing
     consent. ZAŁÓŻ KONTO submit.
   - finish-en-full.png: Same in English ("Hi Anna · Pick a
     therapeutic modality…").

4. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs". The
   client-side popup OAuth code path is reached only on real click
   in a browser; puppeteer doesn't trigger it. Live verification
   of the popup → CreateUser → redirect happens in feature 8's
   Playwright run.

5. Existing /register/therapist/verify-email is unaffected — the
   social path skips the email-verification interstitial because
   Google already verified the address (auth.currentUser
   .emailVerified === true immediately after signInWithPopup).

Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §8.1: "Three social buttons" — for Slice 3 we ship Google;
  Apple + Microsoft helpers exist on auth-provider but render no
  button (will be added once those providers go live in the
  Firebase Console).
- ✓ §8.1 social-path branch: OAuth pop-up → GetUserByFirebaseUID
  → if NotFound, redirect to /register/therapist/finish → submit
  → CreateUser → Trial auto-provisioning by the existing 0a25ac7
  backend flow.
- ✓ §6.5 R1 "One account per email" — account linking is on per
  manual op #64; Firebase auto-links a same-email signup across
  providers, so a user who first signed in via Google won't get
  a second orphan account if they later use email/password.

